        "v": 5,
        "title": "Tree-sitter integration for code parsing",
        "summary": "Added tree-sitter library and language bindings to common package. New codemap module parses source files using tree-sitter queries for TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, C++, PHP, Rust. Includes .scm query files defining tag extraction rules for classes, functions, types. Backend main-prompt.ts updated with debug logging for patch generation.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:15:59.455Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant can now read and understand the structure of source code files written in many programming languages, including TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Ruby, Go, Java, C#, C++, PHP, and Rust. Previously it could only look at text; now it uses a parsing system to identify specific code elements like function names, class definitions, and type declarations. If you opened a supported code file, you would see the assistant correctly recognize and label its core building blocks instead of treating them as plain text. This applies right now to anyone who asks the assistant to analyze or navigate code in these languages.",
