        "title": "getFileTokenScores replaces getExportedTokens with weighted scoring",
        "summary": "Refactored `getExportedTokens` to `getFileTokenScores` in `common/src/codemap/parse.ts`. The new implementation calculates weighted scores based on file depth, line count, and external call frequency using tree-sitter queries. Updated TypeScript tree-sitter queries in `common/src/codemap/tree-sitter-queries/tree-sitter-typescript-tags.scm` to capture identifiers and call expressions for scoring. `npm-app/src/project-files.ts` updated to reflect the new function signature.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T19:16:03.018Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "If you use the feature that scans your project files to understand what code exists, it now ranks files by importance instead of just listing tokens. Files that are deeper in your project, have more lines of code, or are called frequently from other files now get higher scores. You don't see anything new in the interface today because the output is still commented out in the project files tool, but the scoring system is ready to power smarter sorting or prioritization whenever it's turned on.",
